{"name":"Zucchini","hex":"#17462e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zucchini","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A courgette; a variety of squash, Cucurbita pepo, which bears edible fruit.","The edible fruit of this variety of squash."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of zucchino"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zucchini"}],"entries":[{"title":"Zucchini","blocks":[{"text":"Zucchini, courgette, or Cucurbita pepo var. cylindrica is a summer squash, a vining herbaceous plant whose fruit are harvested when their immature seeds and epicarp (rind) are still soft and edible. It is closely related, but not identical, to the marrow; its fruit may be called marrow when mature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg/330px-CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zucchini","wikidata":"Q7533"},{"title":"Zucchini (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Zucchini is a 1982 children's novel by Barbara Dana and illustrated by Eileen Christelow. It was followed by a sequel, Zucchini Out West."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/35/Zucchinibook.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zucchini_(novel)","wikidata":"Q8074974"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Zucchini-Whole.jpg/500px-Zucchini-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Zucchini-Whole.jpg/1280px-Zucchini-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Zucchini-Whole.jpg/500px-Zucchini-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikiped